# The fixture package's docs item — the third kind.
#
# See §20 of docs/design/sdkgen-packages.md. A docs item installs the same
# three things a target does (a definition, components, optionally
# templates) and emits a tree derived from the model; what differs is that
# its destination is a documentation system rather than a language.
#
# `output.path` is left unset, so this item generates IN TREE at
# `<sdk-repo>/wcat/`. The design argues out-of-tree is the normal case for
# real docs items (§20.7.3 — a site's own README collides with the SDK
# repo's); in-tree is used here because it keeps the fixture's assertions
# about generated paths in one volume.

main: kit: docs: wcat: {
  name: key()
  title: 'Widget Catalogue'
  active: true
  base: 'BASE'
}
